---
/**
 * Bhagavad Gita 2.47, set as a closing epigraph rather than a section
 * subtitle: a shloka under a "Selected projects" heading would read as a
 * non-sequitur, but standing alone at the foot of the page it reads as a
 * signature. Devanagari with transliteration and a plain translation, so it
 * is legible to readers of all three.
 */
---

<aside class="epigraph" aria-label="Personal epigraph">
  <p class="deva" lang="sa">कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन</p>
  <p class="translit" lang="sa-Latn">karmaṇy-evādhikāras te mā phaleṣu kadācana</p>
  <p class="gloss">
    To the work alone you have a right, never to its fruits.
    <span class="src">Bhagavad Gita 2.47</span>
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .epigraph {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    text-align: center;
    /* Tighter at the top of the page than it was at the foot: the verse should
       open the page without pushing the name below the fold. */
    padding-block: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 1.9rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .deva {
    font-family: "Noto Serif Devanagari", var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.2vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .translit {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .gloss {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
    max-width: 46ch;
  }
  .gloss .src {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
